course: dictionary
lesson: 11915
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word bursa is one of them. In science, a bursa is a small bag of fluid inside your body. It sits near a joint, like your knee or elbow. «The bursa near his knee stopped the bone rubbing on the muscle.» The bursa works like a cushion.
explain: Bursa can also be a name. «We visited Bursa, a big city in north-west Turkey.» Here Bursa is a place, and it starts with a capital letter. How do you know which meaning is right? Read the words around it. Cushion, joint and knee point to the body. Turkey and visited point to a place.
explain: When a bursa gets swollen and sore, the problem is called bursitis. «Mum's elbow was swollen and sore, so the doctor said it was bursitis.» Swollen means puffed up and bigger than usual. Sore means it hurts. Always check: does the meaning fit the sentence?
fact: A bursa is a small bag of fluid in the body.
fact: A bursa is usually found near a joint, such as the knee or elbow.
fact: A bursa stops bones, muscles and tendons from rubbing against each other.
fact: Bursitis is when a bursa becomes swollen and sore.
fact: «Housemaid's knee» is a name for bursitis of the knee.
fact: Bursa is also a big city in north-west Turkey, and it is written with a capital B.
fact: Bursa can be a noun with the plural bursae or bursas.
exercise: «The bursa near his knee stopped the bone rubbing on the muscle.» What is a bursa? | A cold that makes joints ache | A muscle that bends the knee | *A small bag of fluid that cushions a joint | A type of bone in the leg
exercise: «Mum's elbow was swollen and sore, so the doctor said it was bursitis.» What does bursitis mean? | A broken bone in the arm | A cold in the arm | A strong, healthy joint | *A bursa that is swollen and sore
exercise: «We visited Bursa, a big city in north-west Turkey.» What is Bursa in this sentence? | *A city in north-west Turkey | A small bag of fluid in the body | A cushion for the knee | A type of bone
test: Ella reads «The bursa in his elbow was sore.» What does she know from the word sore? | *It hurts, so the bursa may be swollen | The bursa is a city | The bursa is very happy | The elbow is made of wood
test: Which is the best way to explain a bursa to a friend? | A bone in your arm | A food that grows in Turkey | *A small fluid-filled cushion near a joint | A type of muscle that moves the leg
exam: In «housemaid's knee», which part of the body is sore? | The head | The elbow | *The knee | The foot
